cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CANEOS Statistical Analysis and Figure Generation Code"
message: "If you use this code, please cite the accompanying PLOS Medicine manuscript and this software release."
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "CANEOS Study Group"
  - family-names: "Liu"
    given-names: "Shiyue"
  - family-names: "He"
    given-names: "Yu"
  - family-names: "Lei"
    given-names: "Ruobin"
  - family-names: "Chen"
    given-names: "Yaolong"
  - family-names: "Shi"
    given-names: "Yuan"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible R analysis, site-selection ordering, and figure generation code
  for the China Antibiotics in Neonates with Early-Onset Sepsis
  (CANEOS) multicenter cohort study (2015-2024). Contains statistical code,
  static methodological rule configurations, published aggregate calibration
  weights (S2 Table), and bilingual schema documentation; restricted
  patient-level and hospital-level data are excluded and available through
  institutional ethics approval.
keywords:
  - neonatal early-onset sepsis
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - empirical antibiotic coverage
  - complex survey design
  - reproducible research
  - PLOS Medicine
